{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/the-crossroads-continent/1545940-inktober-postings-and-story-with-art-redux-2","id":1545940,"title":"Inktober postings and story with art Redux #2","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Crossroads Continent"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-15T08:27:23-08:00","id":1545940,"title":"Inktober postings and story with art Redux #2","content":"Inktober Redux2: Continuing to show the art from last month's Inktober extravaganza in the order that the things depicted happened in our D&amp;D game the art is based on.<br /> <br /> Still in our player characters' backstories, as we have the M'udd sea elf siblings escaping the burning wreck of the pirate ship they were crew on, with a couple of fellow crewmembers and the dwarven wizard who had been a prisoner of the pirates. Now, while there is every chance that the term pirates used in the Crossroads Continent means seadogs as awful as in our real world, the way our group is thinking is more like pirates from a popular anime series. So more wacky sea adventures with strange enemies that are other pirates. (Rather than brutality and scurvy.)<br /> <br /> Landing at the port City of the First Horse, the other escaped pirates take off, but the dwarf and the elves duck into a dockside tavern hoping to warm up and hide out from the authorities. And, in fact, the dock guards do enter and start questioning the patrons, until our pirates' new acquaintance, human priest Hugh Vandalay reveals that he is a lesser noble with the papers to prove it and shoos the guards out the door before they can check out the others.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, in the corner, a green-chitined Mantid insect person is playing a lute and his own arm barbs and gathers a small amount of tips as he joins the other PCs. But those tips are stolen in a snatch-n-grab, and the group chases the thief right into an underground series of tunnels that lead to sea caves below the city.<br /> <br /> There's a whole series of playing sessions that didn't get illustrated this time as the Inktober prompts were all about outdoor exploration, but the upshot is that the party defeat a were-rat smuggler and his several gangs of thieves and smugglers and take a small ship. Sailing it through the seacave tunnels clearly used for a long time by smugglers, they discover a side branch and there discover and break through a secret door that has been closed undisturbed for centuries...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}